 of the score differences ranged from <strong>2 to 14 points</strong>. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"656ad12f0b57b5a4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b96abde6e8f69a5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b96abde6e8f69a5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c22ad1353794285\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHow are the NAEP mathematics assessment results reported? Results are reported at grades 4 and 8 as overall average scores on a <strong>0 to 500</strong> scale and as percentages of students performing at or above the NAEP achievement levels: NAEP Basic, NAEP Proficient, and NAEP Advanced.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c22ad1353794285\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a28906c1a6ba594\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a28906c1a6ba594\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"64465102c25090d2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by <strong>lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles)</strong> performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"64465102c2509